{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"heading","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Comparison","type":"heading","anchor":"Comparison","level":3},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"text":"The Decision Rule","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"text":"Hook Selection Guide","type":"heading","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}]},{"text":"Registration Order","type":"heading","anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next Steps","type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"title":"PersistencePlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"title":"SwiduxPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","title":"Security Posture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","title":"PluginHost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","title":"Design Principles"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","title":"Undo \/ Redo"}}}